      "slug": "glow-yarn-a100",
      "term": "Glow yarn",
      "definition": "A yarn blended with a phosphorescent fibre that absorbs light and re-emits it as a soft glow in the dark. In standard room light the yarn appears pale yellow or cream. After 30 seconds in bright light it glows faintly for several minutes. Use it for the firefly tail capsule only; the rest of the body uses regular dk yarn."
    },
    {
      "slug": "tail-capsule-a100",
      "term": "Tail capsule",
      "definition": "A small capsule piece worked as the light organ at the rear of the firefly body. Work 6 dc in a magic ring, increase to 12, work 4 straight rounds, then decrease back to 6 and close. The small size means no stuffing is needed; the yarn holds the shape without fill."
    }
  ],
